WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.570
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:01.860
SPEAKER: If you've
ever felt like you've

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:04.080
had to make a trade-off
between great customer

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.330
support and
operational efficiency,

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:10.100
then Google Cloud's Contact
Center AI is for you.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:13.080
Contact Center AI can
listen, understand,

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.950
and interact in a human-like
manner with your customers.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.080
Contact centers have
a lot of moving parts,

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.090
and so does Contact Center AI.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:22.980
So in this instructional
video, we'll

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.020
provide an overview
of the AI components

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.210
themselves and define
what our partner

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:29.520
solutions can offer
across a range

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.750
of operational environments.

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:33.420
We'll also touch on
the key requirements

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.220
for implementation.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:38.400
Contact Center AI combines
four key ingredients,

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.270
enabling a conversation
that's close to human--

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:46.470
The conversational core, the
Virtual Agent, Agent Assist,

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:48.490
and insights.

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:50.310
Let's jump right in.

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:52.020
Google Cloud's
conversational core

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:54.900
is like a brain that
enables conversation.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:57.810
It redefines the art of
AI-powered conversation

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:00.230
by providing a
close-to-human experience

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:03.990
through Google Cloud's
speech-to-text, a deep learning

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:07.650
neural network API that knows
precisely what customers mean,

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:10.200
regardless of their
accent, use of vocabulary,

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.850
or unique phrasing.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:13.830
Text-to-speech responds
to your customer

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:16.620
in a natural, human-like
manner, allowing the customer

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:20.100
to push the conversation
along, avoiding frustration.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:23.670
Google Cloud's Dialogflow
uses our world-class natural

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:26.820
language understanding to
identify your customer's intent

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.640
and determines the
appropriate next steps.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:31.500
The conversational
core enables you

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:34.320
to provide a consistent,
high quality conversational

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:38.820
experience across channels and
platforms, human and virtual,

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:41.340
which leads us to
the Virtual Agent.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:44.010
A good way to discuss
Google Cloud's Virtual Agent

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:47.630
architecture is to show an
experience we've all had.

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:49.410
Imagine you're the customer.

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:51.870
The conversational
experience begins.

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:53.880
When you initiate
your request, it's

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:56.280
received by Dialogflow,
which matches

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:58.800
the intent after
converting speech to text.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:02.130
The AI also utilizes
optimized telephony models

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:03.290
for the language.

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:05.520
Dialogflow makes a
call to the back end,

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.920
using a web hook function
or other services

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.419
and receives a response.

00:02:09.419 --> 00:02:12.570
This response is then converted
to speech using text-to-speech

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:14.340
and sent back to the user.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:17.160
If your request requires a
deep knowledge-based query,

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:20.760
then the reply is received via
FAQ or a third party knowledge

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:23.100
based service in real
time, providing you

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:25.590
with a seamless
customer experience.

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:28.800
Sometimes a question will still
require live agent support.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:32.100
And Google Cloud's Agent Assist
makes this process seamless

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.090
as well.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:35.860
The call gets routed to an agent
through the partner telephony

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:36.810
channel.

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:39.990
A session manager monitors
the state of the conversation.

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:42.630
It sends the request to
a partner installed agent

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:44.040
desktop.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:45.780
At this point, the
human agent will

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:47.460
see transcripts of
the conversation

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:50.250
with the Virtual Agent, which
saves the agent from having

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:51.840
to repeat questions.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:54.960
Google Cloud's Contact Center
AI with its built-in natural

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:58.110
language understanding grabs
the context of the conversation

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:01.530
to suggest articles and real
time, step-by-step guidance

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:04.590
so the agent can help the
conversation move along.

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:07.920
The human agent is also provided
with smart replies on the Agent

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.150
Desktop.

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:12.150
Agents can also provide feedback
on the article suggestions

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:13.890
so the system can learn.

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:16.440
The conversation experience
is further enhanced

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:19.030
through the insights you'll
gain into your customer data,

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:22.500
including top call drivers
and associated sentiment.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:25.110
You'll be able to upload data
in the form of voice and chat

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:27.000
transcripts that
are then converted

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.310
to text using speech-to-text.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:32.520
Your insights become available
via a live dashboard showing

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:35.760
tons of stats like how many
calls are being received,

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:39.630
what is the percent split
amongst intents, and more.

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:42.420
Up to now, we've focused on the
components of Contact Center

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:43.240
AI.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:46.530
Now, let's talk about how you'll
experience the ground game.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:48.660
Robotic pre-recorded
voices will now

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.330
be human-like,
text-to-speech conversations

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.520
that are generated on the fly.

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:56.210
Rules-based fixed
hierarchy bots are now

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:58.710
AI-powered virtual agents.

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:01.710
Clunky speech transcriptions
requiring regular tuning

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:04.560
are now auto-tuned,
AI-driven speech models,

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:07.710
running on Google's own
neural network TPUs.

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:10.920
And searching knowledge
bases or memorizing shortcuts

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:13.980
will be a thing of the past
by surfacing relevant articles

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:17.529
and insights in real
time to human agents.

00:04:17.529 --> 00:04:20.579
So now you're ready to start
your own implementation.

00:04:20.579 --> 00:04:23.430
Google Cloud has partnered with
your existing telephony partner

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:27.000
to ensure the transition to
Contact Center AI is seamless.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.980
We've done the technical heavy
lifting so you don't have to.

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:32.340
All you need to do is
enable the solution.

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:34.110
Telephony partners
are Google Cloud's

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:36.660
core go-to-market
exclusive sales channel,

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:39.210
with Cloud AI serving
as a critical component

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.770
in their solutions.

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:42.510
Desktop partners
provide the user

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:44.940
interface that the agent
uses while interacting

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:46.150
with the customer.

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:49.230
This interface receives
information from Dialogflow

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:52.770
and will display the transcript
and knowledge as it surfaces.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:55.560
Knowledge partners synchronize
the contact center's content

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:57.360
into the customer's
knowledge bases,

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.610
providing the ability to
surface knowledge articles

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:03.170
and suggestions to human agents,
allowing Google Cloud's Contact

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:05.840
Center AI to provide
access to the customer's

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:09.860
corpus of information at
every agent's fingertips.

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:12.890
Contact Center AI will only
be available for purchase

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:15.320
through Google Cloud's
telephony partners.

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:17.540
However, systems
integration partners

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:20.360
will be utilized for
integrating Contact Center AI

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:23.780
components with the selected
telephony partner platform.

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:26.810
Systems integrators can also
offer complementary services

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:29.280
for on-boarding and
integration beyond what

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:31.490
the telephony partner offers.

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:35.570
Interested in taking the next
steps toward Contact Center AI?

00:05:35.570 --> 00:05:37.910
Talk with your contact
center vendor or Google Cloud

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:39.800
representative to
discuss next steps

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:41.990
for implementing Google
Cloud's Contact Center

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:44.380
AI in your business.

